{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/User Interface.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/User Interface.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"user interface user interface","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/User Interface.md","fileName":"User Interface.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"User Interface","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 13:11\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Human-Computer Interaction Foundations]] · [[Game Interface and Accessibility]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Human-Computer Interaction Foundations","Game Interface and Accessibility","Input Device","Output Device","Interaction Technique","Usability","User Experience","Game Interaction Model","Camera Model","3duserinterfaces2ande.pdf","fundamentalsofgamedesign3e.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/User Interface.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/User Interface.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"user interface user interface","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/User Interface.md","fileName":"User Interface.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"User Interface","heading":"User Interface","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A user interface is the medium through which a person and a computer communicate. It translates user actions and state into inputs the computer can interpret, and translates computer actions and state into outputs the person can perceive and act upon.\n\nA UI includes more than what appears on a screen. Its components can include [[Input Device]]s, [[Output Device]]s, [[Interaction Technique]]s, widgets, and organizing metaphors. The quality of these components and their relationships contributes to [[Usability]] and the broader [[User Experience]].\n\nIn a game, the interface is both a presentation layer and a control system between the real player and the game world. Its [[Game Interaction Model]], [[Camera Model]], visual and audio elements, input devices, and navigation mechanisms jointly determine what the player can perceive and do.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Human-Computer Interaction Foundations","Game Interface and Accessibility","Input Device","Output Device","Interaction Technique","Usability","User Experience","Game Interaction Model","Camera Model","3duserinterfaces2ande.pdf","fundamentalsofgamedesign3e.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/User Interface.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/User Interface.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"user interface user interface","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/User Interface.md","fileName":"User Interface.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"User Interface","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[3duserinterfaces2ande.pdf]]\n\n[[fundamentalsofgamedesign3e.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Human-Computer Interaction Foundations","Game Interface and Accessibility","Input Device","Output Device","Interaction Technique","Usability","User Experience","Game Interaction Model","Camera Model","3duserinterfaces2ande.pdf","fundamentalsofgamedesign3e.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}